  {
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "Adding AI's analysis below: \n=============\nManual offset calculations: The commit replaced:\n   # OLD: Using block pointers (safer)\n   K_block_ptr = tl.make_block_ptr(...)\n   k = load_checked_block(K_block_ptr, ...)\n   \n   # NEW: Manual indexing (error-prone)\n   offs_n_load = kv_base_offset + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)\n   k = load_checked_2d(K, offs_n_load, offs_k, stride_kn, stride_kk, ...)\n  \nPaged attention complexity: Your failing test is specifically test_flex_attention_stride_ordering_mode_paged_attention_permute_order3_shape0_cuda - a paged attention test with stride ordering and permutation. The manual offset calculations introduced in this commit are particularly error-prone for paged attention where memory layout is non-contiguous. \n\nThe illegal memory access is likely occurring because the manual offset calculations (kv_base_offset + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)) may not correctly account for the complex memory layout in paged attention scenarios with stride ordering and permutations.\nRecommendation: Revert commit b36a20d368 or examine the offset calculation logic in forward_block_mn within common.py.jinja, specifically how kv_base_offset and stride calculations interact with paged attention's non-contiguous memory layout.\n\n",
